{
  "paths": {
    "/reduce-colors": {
      "post": {
        "tags": [
          "Cleanup"
        ],
        "summary": "Reduce colors",
        "description": "Quantize images onto a smaller, shared palette.\n\nPixel art reads as pixel art partly because of its restricted palette. AI output\nand converted artwork often carry hundreds of near-identical colors; this snaps\nthem onto a tight palette, optionally with ordered dithering.\n\nPassing several frames in one call is the point of the endpoint: they are\nquantized together, so an animation or a character's eight directions come back\nsharing ONE palette instead of drifting apart frame by frame.\n\nThree ways to choose the palette:\n- omit `num_colors` and `palette_image` — the palette size is auto-detected\n- `num_colors` — quantize to exactly this many colors\n- `palette_image` — reuse the colors of an existing image (your game's palette)\n\nTotal size limit across all frames is 512x512 worth of pixels (e.g. sixteen\n64x64 frames, or four 128x128).\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.pixellab.ai/v2/reduce-colors \\\n    -H \"Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN\" \\\n    -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    -d '{\"images\": [{\"base64\": \"...\"}, {\"base64\": \"...\"}], \"num_colors\": 16}'\n```",
        "operationId": "reduce_colors_endpoint_reduce_colors_post",
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReduceColorsRequest"
              }
            }
          },
          "required": true
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successfully quantized",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ReduceColorsResponse"
                },
                "example": {
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "type": "base64",
                      "base64": "data:image/png;base64,..."
                    }
                  ],
                  "palette": {
                    "type": "base64",
                    "base64": "data:image/png;base64,..."
                  },
                  "n_colors": 16,
                  "usage": {
                    "type": "usd",
                    "usd": 0.005
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Invalid API token"
          },
          "402": {
            "description": "Insufficient credits"
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation error"
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Too many requests"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "/background-jobs/{job_id}": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Jobs"
        ],
        "summary": "Get background job status",
        "description": "Check the status and results of a background job.\n\nThis endpoint allows you to monitor the progress of background operations like\ncharacter creation and animation generation. Background jobs are used for \nexpensive operations that take time to complete.\n\n**Job Statuses:**\n- `processing` - Job is currently running\n- `completed` - Job finished successfully \n- `failed` - Job encountered an error\n\n**Usage Pattern:**\n1. Create a character or animation (returns `background_job_id`)\n2. Poll this endpoint periodically to check status\n3. When status is `completed`, access results in `last_response`\n\n**Response Data:**\n- For character creation: `character_id`, `directions_count`, character info\n- For animations: `animation_id`, `frame_count`, animation details\n- Storage information and file organization details\n\n**Authentication:**\nRequires a valid API token. You can only access jobs you created.\n\n**Error Handling:**\n- 404: Job not found or doesn't belong to you\n- Jobs are automatically cleaned up after completion\n\n**Polling Recommendations:**\n- Poll every 5-10 seconds while status is `processing`\n- Stop polling once status is `completed` or `failed`\n- While `processing`, `last_response.queue_position` and\n  `last_response.estimated_wait_seconds` show a job waiting for a GPU\n- To stop a job, `DELETE /v2/background-jobs/{job_id}`\n- Character creation typically takes 30-60 seconds\n- Animations may take longer depending on frame count and directions",
        "operationId": "get_background_job_status_background_jobs__job_id__get",
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "job_id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "title": "Job Id"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successfully retrieved job status",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BackgroundJobResponse"
                },
                "example": {
                  "id": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000",
                  "status": "completed",
                  "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
                  "last_response": {
                    "character_id": "456e7890-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174001",
                    "saved_to_storage": true,
                    "uploaded_directions": [
                      "south",
                      "east",
                      "north",
                      "west"
                    ],
                    "directions_count": 4
                  },
                  "usage": {
                    "type": "usd",
                    "usd": 0
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Invalid API token"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Job not found or doesn't belong to user"
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Too many requests"
          }
        }
      },
      "delete": {
        "tags": [
          "Jobs"
        ],
        "summary": "Cancel a background job",
        "description": "Cancel a background job that is still `processing`.\n\n- Frees your concurrency slot immediately, so you can submit new work.\n- A job still waiting in the queue is removed and not charged. Billing only\n  covers work a GPU actually did, so a generation that is already running may\n  still finish and be charged.\n- A job you resubmit starts at the back of the queue. While a job is\n  `processing`, `last_response.queue_position` and\n  `last_response.estimated_wait_seconds` (from GET\n  `/v2/background-jobs/{job_id}`) show that it is waiting for a GPU. A waiting\n  job is not stuck, and cancelling it to resubmit makes the wait longer.",
        "operationId": "cancel_background_job_background_jobs__job_id__delete",
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ],
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "job_id",
            "in": "path",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "title": "Job Id"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Job cancelled",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CancelBackgroundJobResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "Job already completed or failed; nothing to cancel"
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Invalid API token"
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "Job not found or doesn't belong to user"
          },
          "409": {
            "description": "Job completed while the cancel was being applied"
          },
          "422": {
            "description": "Validation Error",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/HTTPValidationError"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/balance": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Account"
        ],
        "summary": "Get balance",
        "description": "Returns the current balance for your account, including both USD credits and remaining subscription generations.\n\nUsing the Python client:\n```python\nimport pixellab\n\nclient = pixellab.Client(secret=\"YOUR_API_TOKEN\")\nbalance = client.get_balance()\nprint(f\"Credits: ${balance.credits.usd}\")\nprint(f\"Generations remaining: {balance.subscription.generations}/{balance.subscription.total}\")\n```",
        "operationId": "get_balance_balance_get",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Successfully retrieved balance",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BalanceResponse"
                },
                "example": {
                  "credits": {
                    "type": "usd",
                    "usd": 10.5
                  },
                  "subscription": {
                    "type": "generations",
                    "status": "active",
                    "plan": "Tier 2: Pixel Artisan",
                    "generations": 450,
                    "total": 2000
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Invalid API token"
          }
        },
        "security": [
          {
            "HTTPBearer": []
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "schemas": {
    "ReduceColorsRequest": {
      "properties": {
        "images": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Base64Image"
          },
          "type": "array",
          "minItems": 1,
          "title": "Images",
          "description": "Image(s) to quantize (PNG base64). Several frames are quantized together onto ONE shared palette and must all be the same size — pass an animation's frames or a character's directions in one call so their colors stay consistent."
        },
        "num_colors": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer",
              "maximum": 256,
              "minimum": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Num Colors",
          "description": "Target number of colors. Omit to auto-detect a good palette size from the image itself. Mutually exclusive with palette_image."
        },
        "palette_image": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Base64Image"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "An image whose colors become the palette (max 256 colors). Use it to force frames onto an existing game palette. Mutually exclusive with num_colors."
        },
        "dithering": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "none",
            "2x2",
            "4x4",
            "8x8"
          ],
          "title": "Dithering",
          "description": "Ordered dithering matrix size. Larger matrices give smoother gradients at the cost of a busier look.",
          "default": "none"
        },
        "dithering_strength": {
          "type": "number",
          "maximum": 10,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Dithering Strength",
          "description": "How strongly to dither. Ignored when dithering is 'none'.",
          "default": 5
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "images"
      ],
      "title": "ReduceColorsRequest",
      "description": "Request model for the reduce-colors endpoint",
      "example": {
        "dithering": "none",
        "images": [
          {
            "base64": "iVBORw0KGgoAAAANS..."
          }
        ],
        "num_colors": 16
      }
    },
    "ReduceColorsResponse": {
      "properties": {
        "usage": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Usage"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "example": {
            "type": "usd",
            "usd": 0.02
          }
        },
        "images": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Base64Image"
          },
          "type": "array",
          "title": "Images"
        },
        "palette": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Base64Image",
          "description": "A 1px-tall strip of the resulting palette, most frequent color first. Feed it back as palette_image to lock later frames to it."
        },
        "n_colors": {
          "type": "integer",
          "title": "N Colors",
          "description": "Colors in the quantized result"
        }
      },
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "images",
        "palette",
        "n_colors"
      ],
      "title": "ReduceColorsResponse",
      "description": "Response for a completed quantization"
    },
    "BackgroundJobResponse": {
      "properties": {
        "usage": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Usage"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "example": {
            "type": "usd",
            "usd": 0.02
          }
        },
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Id",
          "description": "Background job ID"
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Status",
          "description": "Current job status (processing, completed, failed)"
        },
        "created_at": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Created At",
          "description": "ISO timestamp when job was created"
        },
        "last_response": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "additionalProperties": true,
              "type": "object"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Last Response",
          "description": "Latest response data from the job"
        }
      },
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "status",
        "created_at"
      ],
      "title": "BackgroundJobResponse",
      "description": "Response model for background job status",
      "example": {
        "created_at": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z",
        "id": "123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000",
        "last_response": {
          "character_id": "456e7890-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174001",
          "character_name": "Fire Wizard",
          "character_prompt": "A powerful wizard with fire magic",
          "directions_count": 4,
          "directions_type": "4-directions",
          "saved_to_storage": true,
          "uploaded_directions": [
            "south",
            "east",
            "north",
            "west"
          ]
        },
        "status": "completed",
        "usage": {
          "type": "usd",
          "usd": 0
        }
      }
    },
    "HTTPValidationError": {
      "properties": {
        "detail": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ValidationError"
          },
          "type": "array",
          "title": "Detail"
        }
      },
      "type": "object",
      "title": "HTTPValidationError"
    },
    "CancelBackgroundJobResponse": {
      "properties": {
        "usage": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Usage"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "example": {
            "type": "usd",
            "usd": 0.02
          }
        },
        "id": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Id",
          "description": "Background job ID"
        },
        "status": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Status",
          "description": "The job's status after the cancel: `failed`"
        },
        "message": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Message",
          "description": "What happened"
        }
      },
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "id",
        "status",
        "message"
      ],
      "title": "CancelBackgroundJobResponse",
      "description": "Response model for a cancelled background job"
    },
    "BalanceResponse": {
      "properties": {
        "credits": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Credits"
        },
        "subscription": {
          "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Subscription"
        }
      },
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "credits",
        "subscription"
      ],
      "title": "BalanceResponse",
      "description": "Response model for balance endpoint"
    },
    "Base64Image": {
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "const": "base64",
          "title": "Type",
          "description": "Image data type",
          "default": "base64"
        },
        "base64": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Base64",
          "description": "Base64 encoded image data"
        },
        "format": {
          "type": "string",
          "title": "Format",
          "description": "Image format",
          "default": "png"
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "type": "object",
      "required": [
        "base64"
      ],
      "title": "Base64Image",
      "description": "A base64 encoded image.\n\nAttributes:\n    type (Literal[\"base64\"]): Always \"base64\" to indicate the image encoding type\n    base64 (str): The base64 encoded image data\n    format (str): The image format (e.g., \"png\", \"jpeg\")"
    },
    "Usage": {
      "properties": {
        "type": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "usd",
            "generations"
          ],
          "title": "Type",
          "default": "usd",
          "example": "usd"
        },
        "usd": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Usd",
          "example": 0.02
        },
        "generations": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "title": "Generations",
          "description": "Number of subscription generations charged (only set when type is 'generations')",
          "example": 1
        }
      },
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "type": "object",
      "title": "Usage",
      "examples": [
        {
          "type": "usd",
          "usd": 0.02
        },
        {
          "generations": 1,
          "type": "generations"
        }
      ]
    },
